<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chad</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chadian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chad is a landlocked country in north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a>. The region around Lake Chad was the heartland of the Kanem-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu Empire</a>, while the east was the home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a>. The area was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the early twentieth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chad.jpg" alt="Chad" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SKopp &amp;amp; others (see upload log) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Chad.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
